  "checks": [
    "Recomputed the six matched comparisons from twelve complete-arm rows. B has lower material U in five pairs, higher material L in six, smaller absolute gap in six and smaller relative gap in six. CITI compact retains P's lower U. Both methods have six qualified fleets, six OPEN arms and zero certificates.",
    "Verified raw signed differences, per-pair normalizations, exact frozen materiality and empty joint-certification speed comparison. Matrix and matched identities give one Native Seed, one thread, one 1200-s complete-process cap, six unique inputs and twelve executed positions.",
    "Matched every displayed new Table 8 and S171.1-S171.4 cell to the arm, input, activity and cost ledgers at the source display precision. Verified narrative counts in the report, decision, memo, main text and Draft PR description.",
    "Verified source-specific geometry and disjointness declarations, the rho=1 weight rule, input-derived T1 and positive floor arithmetic. Final S171 wording states at most one directed nonzero service per station and keeps the route horizon separate from the compute budget.",
    "Re-summed B and P paid clocks, six H calls, 24 LP calls, 16 MIP calls, solver time and audit time. Re-read all raw returned event markers and process exits to verify the final post-Native windows and disjoint evidence-publishing and finalization intervals.",
    "Recomputed B controller totals of zero accepted splits, six declines, maximum one live coverage leaf per arm and four child-target MIP requeues. The manuscript and decision leave independent controller effects unresolved and avoid interpreting endpoint differences as a component effect.",
    "Checked predecessor K1 n50, M-B/ENS n50/n100, R123 long-window n50 and R130/R131 final-S2 scope in pinned sources. The history index retains unresolved schemas and the manuscript uses the six new prospective configurations as a separate denominator.",
    "Compared earlier substantive main and supplement table entries to the Round170 base. They are preserved, with old main Tables 8-11 renumbered 9-12 and cross-references updated. Earlier n15/20/35, PS, resource, weight, full/root, C166, D167 and adverse C169 findings remain in view.",
    "Reviewed EJOR/TRE positioning and the finite OR boundary. Report and manuscript keep the separate earlier Seed evidence, do not infer general scalability or dominance, and retain B as the uniform method.",
    "Opened actual Poppler page images of the exact PDFs. The new table, conclusions, adjacent pages, S171 equations, tables and continuations are legible and unclipped. Checked updated reference numbers, the matrix row label mapping and emitted links to the new ledgers."
  ],
